    description: "Concept audit 2026-10-21/22 (pinned dev e9215548f6; write-up ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept_audit_10212026/concept-audit-vocabulary-since-0923_10222026.md). F4, agent read (two agents independently): builtin is decided by == 'builtin' (taint.py:2328), by 'not community' (verify_claims.py:2309-2312, taint.py:2520), and by path-or-line (io_boundary.py:2455); they agree today only because CI forces every shipped file to declare. DefaultOverlay.provenance '# axis: free-text ... never parsed' (io_boundary.py:2224) is compared as an enum by declares_community (yaml_catalogs.py:288); the runtime validator checks non-empty only (io_boundary.py:2255). PROVENANCE_BUILTIN constant unreferenced (yaml_catalogs.py:278). Fix: one is_builtin predicate, a bounded-enum axis declaration, the validator rejects other values. Also: supply-chain tier 1 doubles as an 'unclassified' sentinel when supply_chain_reason is empty (cli.py:12014-12017, analyze/base.py:1914-1917) although supply_chain_reason is declared never-branch-on free text (ir.py:727) -- make 'unclassified' explicit."  # 735e
