- op: discuss  # ab89
  at: '2026-10-28T07:36:51Z'  # ab89
  by: agent  # ab89
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ab89
  clock: 6  # ab89
  nonce: ab89  # ab89
  message: "Fixed in PR #1914 (90ac53e7e2). yaml_catalogs.declares_builtin is the one rule for a SHIPPED file: builtin only when it declares provenance: builtin, otherwise community (adds, never cleans). catalogue_tiers, split_community_files(shipped=True), shipped_non_boundary_sink_sites and the CLI's loaded-file listing all read it; an operator's own file is still theirs unless it declares community. DefaultOverlay.provenance is declared bounded-enum (it is the tier token), and validate_default_overlays refuses any value but community (it checked non-empty only). Evidence: test_in_repo_catalogues.py::TestOneBuiltinRule (an undeclared shipped file is community in the disclosure and the taint split) and test_default_overlays.py::test_a_default_declares_exactly_community[builtin|Community|pypi.org/requests]; mutating each rule back turned all five red. The rules could only diverge on a malformed shipped file, so no live output changed. Not in scope: the supply-chain tier-1 'unclassified' sentinel half (WI-lidig)."  # ab89
